    "body": "Investigate the general three-polynomial family `u(x)+z*v(x)+z^2*w(x)` in the literal cyclic-source coefficient matrix. The intended result expresses its exact rank through the two minimal degrees of the polynomial recurrence kernel, proves their degree sum after common-factor normalization, and gives a bounded coefficient-matrix procedure to determine them.\n\nThis follows the explicitly open general-kernel question in PR #216 and is distinct from PR #217's special top-coefficient family. Earlier affine and constant-endpoint results retain their credit. There is no unmerged runtime dependency.\n\nThe initial checkpoint records the question and scope. The all-field proof and independent full-source finite controls are in progress. This is an individual-slice classification, not a source-space cap, constructed matrix target, degeneration, or exponent improvement. Keep this PR in draft until its completed evidence and required checks are recorded.",
